  internal/xmlscan/xmlscan.go
      Adapted from go-fast-odf internal/xmlscan (commit 2cf8642), itself
      copied from go-fast-ooxml internal/xmlscan. Extended here for XML in
      general (namespace URIs, offsets, comments, processing instructions,
      the document type declaration, bounded entity expansion, recovery).

  internal/charset (all files, gen/ and testdata/ included)
  internal/entity  (all files)
      Copied from go-fast-html (commit 88e03a0) with only the import path
      changed; internal/charset/stream.go (a streaming DecodeChunk) is
      written here. The provenance of their data tables, as go-fast-html's
      NOTICE gives it, follows.

Data tables taken from specifications, as listed in go-fast-html's NOTICE:

internal/entity/entities.txt
  The named character references of the WHATWG HTML Living Standard,
  section 13.5 "Named character references", whose machine-readable form
  is https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json. The HTML Standard is
  (c) WHATWG (Apple, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft) and licensed under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. The list holds
  the W3C XML Entity Definitions for Characters (the ISO and MathML entity
  sets that DocBook, JATS and TEI DTDs declare) as HTML adopted them.
  internal/entity/gen.go regenerates the file from entities.json.

internal/charset/charset.go (win1252High) and the encoding labels
  From the WHATWG Encoding Standard (index-windows-1252 and the table of
  encoding labels), (c) WHATWG, CC BY 4.0.

internal/charset/tables.go, dbcs.go, cp932.txt, cp936.txt, cp949.txt,
cp950.txt, gen/gen_dbcs.py
  Copied by go-fast-html from go-fast-rtf (internal/codepage, commit
  b756076), same author and licence. tables.go holds the upper halves of
  the single-byte code pages, the content of the Unicode Consortium's
  mapping files MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP874.TXT and CP1250.TXT
  to CP1258.TXT, and MAPPINGS/VENDORS/APPLE/ROMAN.TXT. cp932.txt to
  cp950.txt were generated by gen/gen_dbcs.py from Python's codecs cp932,
  cp936, cp949 and cp950, which implement Microsoft's code pages as the
  Unicode Consortium publishes them. The mapping data is used under the
  Unicode terms of use.

internal/charset/big5-hkscs.txt, gen/gen_big5_hkscs.py
  Generated from Python's cp950 and big5hkscs codecs, (c) Python Software
  Foundation, used under the Python Software Foundation License.

internal/charset/common.go, gen/gen_common.py
  Generated from the Unicode Consortium's Unihan database. Copyright (c)
  1991-2026 Unicode, Inc., Unicode License V3, whose text is in
  LICENSE-UNICODE.

internal/charset/singlebyte.go, gen/gen_single.py
  Generated from the index files of the WHATWG Encoding Standard
  (https://encoding.spec.whatwg.org/), (c) WHATWG, CC BY 4.0.

internal/charset/gb18030-2.txt, gb18030-4.txt, jis0208.txt, jis0212.txt,
gen/gen_cjk_extra.py, and the decoding in cjk.go
  Copied by go-fast-html from go-fast-email v0.2.0, same author and
  licence, where they were generated from Python's gb18030 and cp932
  codecs.

internal/charset/testdata/detect, testdata/text, gen/gen_detect.py
  Texts written for go-fast-html's tests.

Written for this library:

profiles/*.json, profiles/*.md, testdata/profiles/
  The built-in profiles and their notes were written for this library
  from the public documentation of each schema (element and attribute
  names only); no schema, DTD or specification text is included.
  profiles/docbook.json is generated by profile_docbook_test.go from
  testdata/profiles/docbook/rules.json. The sample documents under
  testdata/profiles are synthetic, written for the tests; no corpus file
  is included in this repository.
